# Findings

## High — Required exact-host launch polling remains unimplemented

The verify harness still uses `wait_non_shell_group` with `deadline=$((SECONDS+30))`. It accepts the first non-shell foreground group, fails immediately on an incomplete leader sample, and does not inspect the leader's argv/path. The OpenCode and Pi launch call sites likewise contain no host-specific predicate.

Implement the dispatch requirement directly in the plan and harness: poll fresh `process-info` samples for up to 60 seconds, treating `zsh`, `env`, Bun, wrappers, missing/incomplete leaders, and every nonmatching command as transient. Classify only when the group leader itself matches:

- OpenCode: argv/path equals the owned exact `opencode2.exe` binary.
- Pi: argv command contains the owned Pi root's `node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js`.

The recovery-owned marker and separate exact-PID `lsof` peer poll must occur only after that match. Reflect the same requirement in ordered work and acceptance checks.
